{
  "info": {
    "name": "FixNow Sprint 7.0 Realtime REST Fallback",
    "description": "REST fallback collection for Sprint 7.0 (Realtime).\n\nPostman cannot drive Socket.IO end-to-end; the realtime channel is verified by the gateway unit tests + the React Query bridge unit tests. This collection asserts the REST endpoints that REMAIN the source of truth and the polling fallback that converges the UI when the socket is offline:\n\n  1) GET /v1/me/notifications?experience=provider          — list, paginated\n  2) GET /v1/me/notifications/unread-count?experience=provider — badge count\n  3) GET /v1/provider/conversations                        — chat threads\n  4) GET /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages           — messages history\n  5) POST /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages          — REST-only writes\n  6) GET /v1/provider/available-requests                   — provider feed\n  7) GET /v1/provider/bookings                             — provider bookings\n  8) Negative — no token (401)\n  9) Negative — wrong role (seeker token → 403 on provider feed)\n\nCollection-level guard rejects Prisma / SQL / passwordHash / refreshToken / JWT_SECRET / DATABASE_URL / STRIPE_SECRET leaks on every response.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "fixnow-sprint-7-0-realtime-rest-fallback"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{providerToken}}" }]
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "apiUrl", "value": "http://localhost:4000" },
    { "key": "apiVersion", "value": "v1" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const text = pm.response.text();",
          "pm.test('no Prisma/SQL/secret leak', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.match(/PrismaClient|column .* does not exist|SELECT |INSERT |UPDATE /i);",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('passwordHash');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('refreshToken');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('JWT_SECRET');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('DATABASE_URL');",
          "  pm.expect(text).to.not.include('STRIPE_SECRET');",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1) GET /v1/me/notifications?experience=provider",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/notifications?experience=provider&limit=20"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('items + nextCursor envelope', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('every notification scoped to provider experience', () => {",
              "  for (const n of body.items) {",
              "    if (n.deepLink) pm.expect(n.deepLink.startsWith('/provider/')).to.eql(true);",
              "  }",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2) GET /v1/me/notifications/unread-count?experience=provider",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/me/notifications/unread-count?experience=provider"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('count is a non-negative integer', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.count).to.be.a('number');",
              "  pm.expect(body.count).to.be.at.least(0);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3) GET /v1/provider/conversations",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('items array', () => pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array'));",
              "if (body.items.length > 0) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('conversationId', body.items[0].id);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4) GET /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages?limit=50"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200 or 404', () => pm.expect([200, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.test('items array + nextCursor', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor');",
              "  });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5) POST /v1/provider/conversations/:id/messages (REST-only write)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
          { "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }
        ],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/conversations/{{conversationId}}/messages",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"body\": \"Sprint 7.0 — REST fallback test message\"\n}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 201 or 404', () => pm.expect([201, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
              "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.test('persisted message has id + body + createdAt', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('string');",
              "    pm.expect(body.body).to.eql('Sprint 7.0 — REST fallback test message');",
              "    pm.expect(body.createdAt).to.be.a('string');",
              "  });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6) GET /v1/provider/available-requests",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/available-requests?limit=10"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('items + nextCursor envelope', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7) GET /v1/provider/bookings",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/bookings?limit=10"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('items + nextCursor envelope', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.items).to.be.an('array');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('nextCursor');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8) Negative — no token (GET /v1/provider/bookings → 401)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/bookings"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "pm.test('AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS code', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('AUTH_INVALID_CREDENTIALS'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9) Negative — wrong role (seeker token on provider feed → 403)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{seekerToken}}" }]
        },
        "header": [{ "key": "X-Client-Kind", "value": "mobile" }],
        "url": "{{apiUrl}}/{{apiVersion}}/provider/available-requests"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
              "pm.test('FORBIDDEN code', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('FORBIDDEN'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
